WEBVTT

00:00:00.507 --> 00:00:01.768
Good tools fit us.

00:00:01.884 --> 00:00:03.202
A pen gets a grip.

00:00:03.235 --> 00:00:04.436
A hammer gets a handle.

00:00:04.519 --> 00:00:07.471
A chair gets a backrest, armrests, wheels!

00:00:07.841 --> 00:00:09.672
We keep shaping tools around the people who

00:00:09.722 --> 00:00:10.139
use them.

00:00:10.790 --> 00:00:12.527
So why does software so often work the other

00:00:12.578 --> 00:00:13.475
way around?

00:00:13.543 --> 00:00:14.423
Pick an app.

00:00:14.468 --> 00:00:15.607
Learn its menus.

00:00:15.655 --> 00:00:16.995
Bend your workflow to fit.

00:00:17.080 --> 00:00:18.620
And when your needs change...

00:00:18.654 --> 00:00:19.297
start again.

00:00:19.925 --> 00:00:21.847
What if your tools could change with you?

00:00:21.910 --> 00:00:23.202
That's Tabletop.

00:00:23.240 --> 00:00:24.348
Describe what you need.

00:00:24.383 --> 00:00:25.321
Review the change.

00:00:25.365 --> 00:00:27.545
Put it to work, right on the canvas.

00:00:27.593 --> 00:00:28.760
Then keep shaping it.

00:00:29.456 --> 00:00:30.560
Let's start small.

00:00:30.704 --> 00:00:31.823
A coffee stand.

00:00:31.887 --> 00:00:34.095
Type: Make me a sales table for coffee and

00:00:34.167 --> 00:00:34.853
cake.

00:00:34.909 --> 00:00:37.197
Review the draft, apply it, and you're ready

00:00:37.245 --> 00:00:38.424
to log sales.

00:00:39.617 --> 00:00:40.587
Now the rush hits.

00:00:40.713 --> 00:00:42.967
Typing every sale is slowing you down.

00:00:43.207 --> 00:00:45.418
So you ask for quick-sale buttons.

00:00:46.794 --> 00:00:46.942
Review.

00:00:47.039 --> 00:00:47.813
Apply.

00:00:47.861 --> 00:00:49.048
Click Coffee...

00:00:49.092 --> 00:00:51.228
four coffees, and the total updates.

00:00:51.315 --> 00:00:52.099
Same table.

00:00:52.201 --> 00:00:53.044
Less work.

00:00:54.448 --> 00:00:55.162
What's selling?

00:00:55.226 --> 00:00:56.100
Add a chart.

00:00:56.136 --> 00:00:58.300
Review it, apply it, and it reads the sales

00:00:58.336 --> 00:00:58.949
already here.

00:00:59.117 --> 00:01:00.175
No copying.

00:01:00.223 --> 00:01:01.257
No starting over.

00:01:02.396 --> 00:01:03.924
Time for an afternoon offer.

00:01:04.068 --> 00:01:06.050
Add a ten-percent discount.

00:01:06.107 --> 00:01:07.527
Review, apply...

00:01:07.575 --> 00:01:09.545
gross stays at two hundred and fifty.

00:01:09.618 --> 00:01:11.563
Net: two hundred and twenty-five.

00:01:12.923 --> 00:01:13.360
Actually...

00:01:13.388 --> 00:01:14.657
make that twenty percent.

00:01:14.801 --> 00:01:17.899
Select the rule, ask for the change, and check

00:01:17.936 --> 00:01:18.764
the preview.

00:01:18.861 --> 00:01:19.413
Apply.

00:01:19.557 --> 00:01:21.070
Net: two hundred.

00:01:21.142 --> 00:01:23.376
The table, buttons, and chart stay put.

00:01:24.567 --> 00:01:25.847
Start with what you need.

00:01:25.937 --> 00:01:26.527
Use it.

00:01:26.630 --> 00:01:27.487
Change it.

00:01:27.599 --> 00:01:28.527
Keep going.

00:01:28.674 --> 00:01:29.967
Tabletop.

00:01:30.047 --> 00:01:31.807
Tools that adapt to you.
